{
  "case_id": "2020-20-366",
  "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case should be over. The district court held that appellees would be injured because illegal aliens would be chilled from participating in the enumeration. But that counting is now over, and whatever chill ever existed has fallen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Census Bureau",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "by December 31, and then, by January 11, the Census Bureau says that it intends to provide the President with the information \"necessary to fully implement the Presidential Memorandum.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, if -- if an undocumented person has been in the country for, say, 20 years, you know, even if illegally, as you say, why would some person not have a -- such a person not have a settled residence here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Constitution and laws require the seats in the House be apportioned according to the number of persons in each state. The President's new policy of refusing to count people who are not in a lawful immigration status is flatly inconsistent with that command."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what does that accomplish? Because I thought your -- your -- your major concern is the use of that information by the President."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first concerns your answer that it would be fine for the Secretary of Commerce to submit numbers that exclude illegal aliens if it was done in a separate document."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "exclude illegal aliens, we have to decide as a matter of law whether the word \"person,\" as used in the statute and Constitution, who live here permits the exclusion of illegal aliens, correct? That's the legal question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it is a matter of speculation whether they're going to be able to include or exclude, why isn't that a standing problem or a ripeness problem now, if -- if we must rule now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Private Appellants",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "we have Article III standing. We have a substantial risk."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So is it your position that every single person who is in -- every single alien who is in the United States on census day must be counted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0004-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Census Bureau had determined based on experience that administrative record to which it already had access would enable it to determine citizenship status for approximately 90 percent of the population."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0004-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think, when you add all of that together, that's at least a substantial risk of injury, because it doesn't take much to change"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How -- how do we think about feasibility?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Latino justice amicus",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0004-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As the Latino justice amicus brief notes, undocumented immigrants contribute $1 trillion in GDP, $20 billion in federal taxes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-366",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "227cc5b1b282b47b5bfa55e8877e53f837168f9943f77b19850e573a9c48da6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-227cc5b1b282-0004-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 98,
        "start": 98
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, General. The case is submitted."
    },
